Subject: [PATCH] Remove unused counter from repeating-call output validation

CallSiteAnalyzer::ensureValidRepeatingCall iterates output operands through
OperandRange2D. Its loop counter is never read, including in assertion-enabled
builds. GCC 16.2.1 rejects the pass with -Werror=unused-but-set-variable.

Remove only the unused declaration and increment. Keep range advancement,
termination, output tracking, and duplicate-output rejection unchanged.
No compiler warning option is changed.

Regression: check-repeating-calls.py compiles the actual translation unit
using Ninja's generated command, then repeats with assertions enabled.
The original source fails the release compile with the expected diagnostic.

--- a/src/vpux_compiler/src/dialect/VPUIP/transforms/passes/legalize_repeating_func_calls.cpp
+++ b/src/vpux_compiler/src/dialect/VPUIP/transforms/passes/legalize_repeating_func_calls.cpp
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@
             const bool firstTimeSeenValue = memorizedOutputs.insert(*x).second;
             return !firstTimeSeenValue;
         };
-        for (size_t i = 0; !argsAcrossCallSites.empty(); OperandRange2D::advance(argsAcrossCallSites), ++i) {
+        for (; !argsAcrossCallSites.empty(); OperandRange2D::advance(argsAcrossCallSites)) {
             const auto ithOutputs = argsAcrossCallSites.get();
             auto it = llvm::find_if(ithOutputs, visitValue);
             // this is currently not supported
